    <div class="article-intro"><div class="article-hero"><img src="/assets/blog/custo-recarga.webp" width="1280" height="720" alt="Property manager reviews EV charging consumption and cost allocation" fetchpriority="high"></div><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal"></span>VeVolt guide</p><h1>How to allocate EV charging costs in a condominium</h1><p class="lede">Transparent allocation starts with a known source for consumption, an agreed rate and a consistent closing period. VeVolt can organize manually entered records, but it does not meter or bill energy.</p><p class="article-meta">Updated 03/08/2026 · 1 min read</p></header></div>
    <div class="article-layout"><div class="article-body"><section><h2>Define the source and formula</h2><p>Document where session consumption comes from, which energy rate applies and how losses or other approved costs are handled. The method should be reproducible by the building administration.</p></section><section><h2>Review records before charging residents</h2><p>Check missing sessions, duplicate values, units and discrepancies against the building&#39;s chosen source. VeVolt records are operational support, not an electricity invoice.</p><ul><li>Closing period</li><li>Consumption source</li><li>Approved rate</li><li>Review owner</li><li>Documented adjustments</li></ul></section><section><h2>Keep an auditable closing process</h2><p>Keep supporting readings and approvals in the condominium&#39;s official records. The app helps consolidate manually entered sessions for monthly review.</p></section><nav class="article-context-links" aria-label="Continue the condominium charging guide"><h2>Continue the condominium charging guide</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/condo">Organize manual allocation with VeVolt Condo</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/electric-car-charger-in-condominium">Read the pillar guide</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/condominium-ev-charging-management">Structure the complete management workflow</a></li></ul></nav><section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item"><summary>Does VeVolt read a meter?</summary><p>No. Consumption and costs are entered manually.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Does VeVolt collect payment?</summary><p>No. Billing and payment happen outside the app.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Who chooses the rate?</summary><p>The condominium must define and validate its method for the local context.</p></details></div></section></div>
    <aside class="article-aside"><h2>Organize with VeVolt Condo</h2><p>Organize residents, schedules, sessions and manual cost allocation with VeVolt Condo. Eligible new customers can try the monthly plan free for 15 days on Google Play.</p><a class="play-badge-link" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=br.com.vevolt" rel="noopener" aria-label="Get it on Google Play"><img src="/assets/google-play-badge-en.png" width="564" height="168" alt="Get it on Google Play"></a><h2>Sources and further reading</h2><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://www.gov.br/aneel/pt-br/assuntos/veiculos-eletricos" rel="noopener noreferrer">ANEEL - Electric vehicles and charging rules</a></li><li><a href="https://www.gov.br/inmetro/pt-br/acesso-a-informacao/perguntas-frequentes/avaliacao-da-conformidade/etiquetagem-para-veiculos-leves/como-e-calculado-o-consumo-dos-carros-eletricos" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inmetro - How electric-vehicle consumption is calculated</a></li></ul></aside></div>
